# The SKILLS the release ships — a NAME-LEVEL manifest, deliberately not part
# of files: above. A skill's prose is yours to adapt from the moment bootstrap
# installs it, so the byte question the shared layer answers ("is my copy
# verbatim?") is the wrong one here; the only question this list answers is
# "does my project HAVE every skill this release ships?" — and it answers it
# as STATE, so an update from any older release, however many windows were
# skipped, still yields the exact missing list. Only the first word of an
# entry is the name; anything after it is annotation. One skill is optional
# (bootstrap asks before installing it) — declining it is a clean state, not
# a gap.
skills:
  diagnose
  dogfood            optional — bootstrap asks; declining is a recorded choice
  explain-diff
  grill-me
  grill-with-docs
  implement
  improve-codebase-architecture
  merge-train
