# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEVIATION FROM THE SHARED LAYER (centaur-spec) — recorded, not hidden.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two files above are listed as shared layer but are, in THIS repo, a RECORDED
# LOCAL FORK — they exist at the pinned paths (so `scripts/check.sh` is
# satisfied), but their CONTENT diverges from v0.12.0 on purpose:
#
#   scripts/docs-conformance/context.mjs   the v0.12.0 context VERBATIM plus a
#                                          local `paths` map on the returned ctx
#                                          (the eight local validators read it).
#                                          list/read/exists/config are unchanged,
#                                          so the shared validators run against it.
#   scripts/docs-conformance/runner.mjs    registers ELEVEN validators, not the
#                                          three v0.12.0 ships: the kit's
#                                          claude-md-refs + skill-web + skill-paths
#                                          PLUS eight local docs-skeleton
#                                          validators (adr-index-sync, adr-madr,
#                                          glossary-terms, event-names,
#                                          feature-presence, feature-executes,
#                                          gherkin-structure, openapi-structure).
#
# Why: centaur-spec adopted the docs-conformance engine before v0.10.0 and grew
# eight local validators that read `ctx.paths`. v0.10.0 upstreamed only
# `claude-md-refs` and deleted both the extra validators and `ctx.paths`; 0.11.0
# and 0.12.0 then ADDED `skill-web` and `skill-paths` to the shared layer. Taking
# runner.mjs/context.mjs verbatim would silently drop the eight checks this repo
# depends on, so they stay forked while `index.mjs` and every
# `validators/*.mjs` the kit ships (claude-md-refs, skill-web, skill-paths) are
# taken verbatim and registered alongside the local eight. When the kit
# upstreams the docs-skeleton validators (its runner.mjs comment names this as
# planned work), this fork can retire. See docs/diary.md and
# constitution/local-workflow.md for the same note in prose.
#
# The `skills:` manifest above is the kit's shipped set, taken wholesale. This
# repo's own installed set deviates by name in two recorded ways: it ships
# `ce-dogfood` where the kit ships the optional `dogfood`, and (as of this
# update) it now carries `explain-diff`. The skills' BODIES are adapted to this
# stack throughout (ADR numbers, this repo's tools) — expected for a non-shared,
# name-level manifest.
